⚙️ What is gRPC?
gRPC (Google Remote Procedure Call) is a high-performance, open-source framework developed by Google that allows services to communicate with each other.

It’s often used instead of REST for faster, more efficient communication between microservices — especially in high-scale systems.

🔍 gRPC vs REST (Why Use gRPC?)
| Feature            | **gRPC**                               | **REST**                        |
| ------------------ | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| 📝 Protocol        | HTTP/2 + **Protocol Buffers** (binary) | HTTP/1.1 + JSON (text)          |
| 📦 Payload size    | **Small** (compressed binary)          | Larger (JSON is text-based)     |
| 🚀 Speed           | **Very fast**                          | Slower due to JSON parsing      |
| 🔄 Streaming       | ✅ Supports bidirectional streaming     | ❌ Limited (manual hacks needed) |
| 🛠 Code generation | ✅ Auto-generates client/server code    | ❌ Manual                        |
| 🌐 Browser support | ❌ Not directly (need proxy)            | ✅ Native                        |


✅ When is gRPC used in Microservices?
When services need high performance (low latency, high throughput)

For internal communication between microservices (within your backend)

For real-time data exchange (like live chat, video calls)

In systems with polyglot architecture (e.g., Java <--> Go <--> Python)

📘 Example Use Case
Let’s say you have these services:

AuthService (Java)

UserService (Python)

NotificationService (Go)

Using gRPC, they can talk to each other seamlessly using Protocol Buffers with generated clients, without worrying about manual REST API integration.

🧪 Bonus: Sample .proto file
proto
Copy
Edit
syntax = "proto3";

service UserService {
  rpc GetUser(UserRequest) returns (UserResponse);
}

message UserRequest {
  string userId = 1;
}

message UserResponse {
  string name = 1;
  string email = 2;
}
From this, gRPC can auto-generate Java, Go, Python, or C# code.

✅ Summary
| Concept               | gRPC                                          |
| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| Type                  | Remote procedure call                         |
| Used for              | Fast, efficient microservice communication    |
| Language support      | Multi-language (Java, Go, Python, etc.)       |
| Better than REST when | You need performance and streaming            |
| Not ideal for         | Browser-based or public APIs (REST is better) |

